    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70-a4">

                <pb facs="0144" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/>

                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to the Prince de la Tour d’Auvergne.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 1, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Washburne, minister of the United States, presents his respectful compliments
                    to his excellency the Prince de la Tour d’Auvergne, minister of foreign affairs,
                    and begs to inclose him a dispatch, which he has just received from Mr. Motley,
                    the minister of the United States in London, and which explains itself.</p>
            </div>
